Zanele: The older ones are ready for more than I can give them. That is a good problem and it is still a problem.
- What do they need?
	Hope: What do they need?
	Zanele: A teacher who studied past what I studied. Someone who knows where mathematics goes after the part I can take them to.
	Zanele: I have been at the edge of my own education for about four years now. I keep half a page ahead of the brightest one in the room.
	Zanele: That is a sentence I have not said out loud to anybody. Please do not repeat it.
